    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1634">

                <pb facs="1185" n="1069" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1069"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/682.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the French
                        Ambassador.</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d1634-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to previous
                    correspondence in regard to the protection of French interests in Mexico, I beg
                    to <pb facs="1186" n="1070" xml:id="pg1070"/> inform you that the Department is
                    in receipt of two telegrams from its representative at Torreon, in which he
                    states that the de facto Government of Mexico has informed him that, in matters
                    concerning the interests of foreign governments, it desires to deal directly
                    with accredited representatives of those governments.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1634-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d1634-f1-content">
                <p>The same, mutatis mutandis, to the British, German, and Italian Ambassadors; and
                    on October 23 to the Spanish Ambassador (see under Protection of Spanish
                    interests).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
